sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Editor as Editorial operator
    participant CLI as run_pipeline.py
    participant Pipeline as Pipeline orchestrator
    participant Parser as XML parser
    participant Rules as Rule detectors
    participant GPT as IntelliHub / GPT-OSS
    participant Templates as Template detector
    participant Risk as Risk engine
    participant Reports as Report writer

    Editor->>CLI: Start batch with input, dictionary, output, and flags
    CLI->>Pipeline: Build PipelineConfig and run
    Pipeline->>Parser: Discover sorted XML files recursively

    loop Every XML file
        Parser->>Parser: Parse supported schema and split sub-articles
        Parser->>Parser: Normalize metadata and abstract sections
        Parser->>Parser: Exclude author, affiliation, reference, and table blocks
        Parser-->>Pipeline: ParsedRecord plus warnings and exclusion audit
    end

    Pipeline->>Pipeline: Remove exact duplicates and disambiguate ID collisions
    Pipeline->>Rules: Compile built-in LLM rules and tortured-phrase dictionary

    loop Every retained record
        par Deterministic checks
            Pipeline->>Rules: Detect explicit LLM response traces
        and
            Pipeline->>Rules: Detect known tortured phrases
        end
        Rules-->>Pipeline: Evidence-backed deterministic findings

        opt --detect-nonsense-candidates
            Pipeline->>Pipeline: Keep unmatched sentences passing local prefilters
            Pipeline->>GPT: Review one candidate sentence as untrusted text
            GPT-->>Pipeline: Strict JSON sentence verdict
            Pipeline->>Pipeline: Add low-severity candidate only when not understandable
        end
    end

    Pipeline->>Pipeline: Sort findings and assign run-local finding IDs

    opt --validate-llm
        loop Every LLM-trace or tortured-phrase finding
            Pipeline->>GPT: Validate matched phrase in its evidence context
            GPT-->>Pipeline: confirmed, rejected, or uncertain plus reason
            Pipeline->>Pipeline: Annotate finding without suppressing it
        end
    end

    Pipeline->>Templates: Compare all retained records within the current batch
    Templates-->>Pipeline: Candidate clusters, scores, peers, and exclusions
    Pipeline->>Risk: Aggregate raw findings plus template membership per record
    Risk-->>Pipeline: None, Low, Medium, or High plus review flag
    Pipeline->>Reports: Supply records, findings, clusters, warnings, and metadata
    Reports-->>Editor: Canonical JSON and Editor_Triage_Workbook.xlsx

    Note over GPT,Risk: GPT validation annotations never alter deterministic risk
